AIM:- Implement a first in first out (FIFO) queue using only two stacks. The implemented queue should support all the functions of a normal queue (push, peek, pop, and empty).

ALGORITHM :- 
 Queue Using Two Stacks

Let the two stacks be S1 and S2.

push(x)
Push the new element x into S1.
This stores elements in the order they arrive.
pop()
If S2 is empty:
Move all elements from S1 to S2 one by one.
The top of S2 is now the oldest element.
Pop and return the top element of S2.
peek()
If S2 is empty:
Move all elements from S1 to S2.
Return the top element of S2 without removing it.
empty()
Check whether both S1 and S2 are empty.
If both are empty, return true.
Otherwise, return false.

CODE:-
class MyQueue {
public:
    stack<int> s1, s2;

    MyQueue() {
    }

    void push(int x) {
        s1.push(x);
    }

    int pop() {
        if (s2.empty()) {
            while (!s1.empty()) {
                s2.push(s1.top());
                s1.pop();
            }
        }
        int x = s2.top();
        s2.pop();
        return x;
    }

    int peek() {
        if (s2.empty()) {
            while (!s1.empty()) {
                s2.push(s1.top());
                s1.pop();
            }
        }
        return s2.top();
    }

    bool empty() {
        return s1.empty() && s2.empty();
    }
};
